    "leafs": {
      "full_name": "Toronto Maple Leafs",
      "league": "NHL",
      "record": "32-36-14",
      "detail": "8th in Atlantic Division",
      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "The season didn't just slip away - it unraveled, and the final numbers say it all: a <strong>32-36-14</strong> finish, <strong>8th in the Atlantic Division</strong>, <strong>78 points</strong>, and a grim <strong>L7</strong> that left the club buried at <strong>15th</strong> in the playoff seedings. <strong>The latest blow was the Avalanche's 6-3 win in Toronto, a night that summed up the whole mess - too loose, too leaky, too little pushback.</strong> That is not a one-game story so much as the verdict on a team that never found a reliable spine, never dragged itself out of the mud, and spent the spring looking like a roster in need of sharper edges and a harder identity. The Leafs now head into a summer that has to be about decisions, not declarations: the coaching chair will draw scrutiny, the front office has to weigh free agency with care, and the draft board matters more than slogans. There is talent here, but talent without structure is just expensive noise. <strong>What matters next is whether Toronto uses this wreckage to reset the bench, remake the supporting cast, and finally build a team that can survive pressure instead of folding under it.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated May 28, 2026"
      },
